WEBVTT

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:10.440
Established in the Muromachi Era 
Sawaki Souemon
Registered Trademark

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.090
Our grandsons must be 
at the entrance ceremony

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.440
in Tokyo right about now.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.450
Yuuki Brewery

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.330
What's so great about it?

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.450
They're just going to 
the outskirts of Tokyo.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.170
Well, young people want to have fun.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.750
It's good for them.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.700
And it sets me at ease to know 
your Kei-kun is there, too.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:26.460
I wonder what sorts of things 
Tadayasu will see in Tokyo?

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.930
Come to think of it, 
didn't he say he could see microbes?

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.340
Do you believe him?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.930
What grandpa wouldn't believe 
what his own grandson says?

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.000
Besides, I've seen it...

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:50.780
Tadayasu, playing in the cellar 
with something I couldn't see.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.710
Moyashimon

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.950
The Story of the 
Agricultural University Microbes

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.410
Self-Sufficiency

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.360
Care to dedicate your youth 
to the path of acting?

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.410
Drama

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.910
You there! Join the drama club and...

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.210
Kei, why are there police 
at an entrance ceremony?

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.710
Looks like they're handing out flyers.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.360
First of all, to our new students,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.900
congratulations on your acceptance.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.160
15th Outdoor Entrance Ceremony

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.150
I'm Gotou, the university president.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.350
Thanks to your support,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.700
our school of practical 
learning has the honor today

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.570
to commence with the 15th year

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.040
of our traditional outdoor 
entrance ceremony.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.400
Agriculture is one of the most vital

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.780
elements in the propagation of culture

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.700
and preservation of our nation's 
natural environments.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.700
Tokyo's sky is so high...

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.510
Our lifestyles cannot thrive 
without agriculture,

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.250
nor would our country be what it is.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.560
Agriculture will exist as 
long as mankind lives.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.960
We interrupt to bring you a message 
from the university office staff.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.950
As I believe all new 
students are aware

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.140
after receiving the flyers from the police,

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.460
one of our graduate students, 
Hasegawa Haruka-san, is missing.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.460
As she has not been seen in a month,

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:31.480
the investigation is open 
to the public as of today.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.320
Missing  
Hasegawa Haruka-san  
We are looking for this person.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.960
Features: 
Black skirt  
Black boots  
Heavy makeup  
Fair complexion

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.860
Forgive me for bringing this up 
at this lovely entrance ceremony,

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.980
but our school grounds 
are quite expansive.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.940
She may even be buried somewhere.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:44.480
But if you see her, please contact 
the police or the university office.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.460
Yeah, it's been really hard 
since our manager quit...

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.620
What kind of entrance ceremony was that?

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:56.130
Did that office staff guy 
think he was being funny?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.150
Well, it did have an impact.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.460
The subject of the missing 
person will stay

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.130
on people's minds more 
than anything else.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:02.940
Still, calling in the police just

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.030
because they can't get in touch with her?

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.030
Please help us out!

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.560
They're just being paranoid.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.370
She's probably just off with some guy.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.840
Well, the school itself is 
in the rural outskirts,

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.650
but this is still Tokyo.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.610
Oh, crap. Grandpa told 
me to find this guy.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:20.110
Find Professor 
Itsuki Keizou 
of the agricultural 
department.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.740
Professor Itsuki?

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.110
An old friend of his?

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:24.580
No, I've never heard Grandpa 
mention any friends in Tokyo.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.030
Then, want to go meet him first?

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.650
Care to join the tennis club?

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.070
But I wanted to check out 
some clubs, too...

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:35.520
Excuse me, can you tell me where 
Professor Itsuki's office is?

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.040
You work fast...

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.040
Memorial Tower

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.810
What a pain.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.350
Just think of it as a chance 
to explore the campus.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.840
But isn't this thing so hard, 
no one could eat it?

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.260
It's only good for showing

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.140
the new students and 
freaking them out.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.540
That's huge...

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.440
Livestock coming through!

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.440
Priority passage requested!

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:05.540
All right!

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.330
There!

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:09.760
That's it. Great job.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.790
I think I could scoop up 
any kind of dung now!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.000
Keep it up!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:13.660
All right, let's head to the next one.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.770
Damn, these protective suits are hot.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.790
It's for class credits! Tough it out!

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.690
Is everyone like this at college?

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.560
I think you'd only see stuff like 
this at an agricultural university.

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:31.560
Central Square  

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.520
I can feel my image of 
Tokyo colleges crumbling.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.850
Still, I never thought you'd enter 
an agricultural university.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.130
I could say the same for you.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.520
Why did you come here?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.530
Well, I had my reasons.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.910
In my case, this was the only school

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:48.720
in Tokyo that my dad would let me attend.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.900
He still remembers how my brother 
went to college in Tokyo

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:53.350
and got a job in the city right away.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.140
What?

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:58.670
Nothing...

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.170
Anyway, I guess your dad needs you

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.170
to take over the mold-starter business.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:05.370
Gimme a break.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.360
Who wants to work a job surrounded 
by microbes all the—

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:11.930
Um, Kei...

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.760
Do we have to go that way?

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.220
Yeah.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.520
It's supposed to be a shortcut.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:18.390
It just seems like

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:21.200
there are a lot of microbes 
coming from up ahead.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.270
They've been drifting 
this way for a while.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.550
Sorry. Let's take a 
different route, then.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:28.130
You haven't talked about them lately,

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.910
so I thought you couldn't 
see them anymore.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.400
Well, I don't see them 
as much as I used to.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.190
It's been a long time 
since I saw this many.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.410
Oh...

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.600
Maybe there's a dead 
animal or something?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.670
Ah, it's okay. 
I'm not that worried about it.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.840
That's a really strange 
ability, though...

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.420
being able to see microbes.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.430
Sawaki?

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:56.560
Wh-What is that?!

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.430
What?

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.210
It just looks like a pile of dirt to me.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:03.810
So, there must be something buried here.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.330
I wonder what it is.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:09.950
Looks like it'd be about 1.5-2 meters.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.570
About the size of a human.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:14.450
A human?

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:16.700
There's something stuck in the dirt...

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.210
Hasegawa

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.810
Hasegawa?

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.260
Step back, please!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:26.090
Students, please step back!

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.890
Hey, get me a shovel.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:29.110
What is this sign?

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.720
It looks like a pet's grave.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.220
What's that about microbes?

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:35.260
I mean... well...

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:38.130
He has a very sensitive nose.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:40.790
He said something smelled bad, so...

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:44.240
We'll dig it up, and if 
we do find something,

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.810
we'll be talking to you again.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.190
Tokyo police are scary.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.820
Yeah, the officers back home 
usually wore track suits.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.500
But, Sawaki, even if you tell 
people you can see microbes,

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.580
nobody will believe you.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:00.180
I sort of panicked.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.830
Hi, Professor Itsuki!

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:16.300
Hey!

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.560
That stinks!

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.390
What is that stench?!

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:25.810
They're flying out now!

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.080
That reeks!

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.950
Smells like something died!

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:41.120
Do you boys know what this is?

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.250
It's a seal carcass.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.510
What a shame.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.020
You can't tell the difference 
between the smell of lactic acid

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:55.760
fermentation and the smell of decay either?

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.050
Fermentation?

00:08:58.050 --> 00:09:00.010
Are you saying this is something to eat?

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.800
Now that you mention it, 
I think I read about this somewhere.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.020
Is this a fermenting seal?

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:07.970
Indeed.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:11.280
It's a fermented product of the 
Canadian Inuits called kiviak.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:12.660
I knew it.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.780
Wait, someone's going to eat this seal?

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:19.160
No, there are 70 or 80 sea 
birds stuffed in its belly.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:21.740
And... you wouldn't believe it,

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.910
but you suck the bird's innards 
out through its anus.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:32.760
Hmm... the hints of rice bran 
and natto blend beautifully

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:36.800
with that distinctly rich, 
animalistic flavor.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:41.450
One could call this mixture 
of all fermented food flavors

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:44.310
the wisdom of the human race itself.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.260
The people of the Arctic countries 
originally ate raw meat

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.810
to make up for their 
lack of vegetables...

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.220
But eventually, cooking meat 
became an established practice,

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:58.570
leaving them unable to obtain 
the vitamins found in raw meat.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:04.550
So, seasoning cooked 
meat with this kiviak

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:06.790
was useful as a vitamin supplement.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.700
In short, the people of 
the Arctic countries

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:13.690
obtained their vitamins 
through the rich nutrients

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:16.470
produced in fermentation 
by microorganisms.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.710
<i>Bad breath!</i>

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.350
Sawaki Souemon Tadayasu-kun.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:25.220
I'm Itsuki Keizou.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:30.030
I've known your grandfather 
for about 20 years.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.110
And you must be Yuuki Kei-kun.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.110
Starting today, you are my students.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:37.660
Here, have some.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:38.580
No way!

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:39.640
That's right!

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:41.490
You think I'll let you eat that?

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:51.250
That's a very important component 
of my research, Professor!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.280
Ah, Hasegawa-kun, welcome back.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.630
Hasegawa?!

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:06.250
Hasegawa 
Experiment in Progress

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.700
Honestly!

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.270
Why did you open the 
kiviak before I got back?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.290
Well, whenever you're 
away doing research,

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:10.640
I can't get in touch with you.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.840
I did this experiment in my own name!

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.390
You should have waited for me!

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.000
It's Hasegawa.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.420
Yeah, it's Hasegawa.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:16.980
I'm sorry.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:20.720
But you came back at the perfect time.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:24.660
You two, come with us to 
my research lab for now.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.740
Uh, Hasegawa-san...

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:29.320
The police are looking for you.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:31.620
Oh, my dad is just being paranoid.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.950
I stopped by home on my way back here,

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:36.260
so everything's fine.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:37.550
So everything's fine.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.630
I see.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:41.110
Oh, yes... Hasegawa-kun,

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:43.050
this is Sawaki-kun, the one 
we've heard so much about.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.550
Really? So you're...

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.190
Agricultural Department Building

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.940
Welcome to my research lab.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.030
Yeah...

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:00.190
Microorganism Research I  

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.190
Thanks.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:03.360
Sawaki-kun, forgive me for being abrupt,

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:06.830
but Hasegawa here seems 
eager to see your ability.

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:11.710
Grandpa even told you about that?

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:13.330
So you don't deny it?

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:17.210
Well, it's natural to be skeptical 
when I say I can see microbes.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:20.100
You want to know, too, don't you?

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:24.470
Well, all I can think is that 
it's amazing if it's true...

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:27.470
Would you take a look 
at some things for me?

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.230
Hey, it's Tadayasu!

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:36.480
A.    oryzae

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.780
Wow, it is!

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.480
Oh, it's just Tadayasu?

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:39.730
Oh... it's miso made 
at my family's store.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:45.240
Man, and I came to Tokyo to get 
away from this nasty smell...

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.240
Don't close it! Tadayasu!

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.620
Hey, how can you be so sure 
it's your family's miso?

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.170
Because it was our malts in there.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:58.700
So you insist that you can see microbes.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:12:59.880
Well, I can.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.820
All right, if you're so sure...

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:06.290
Professor, could you bump up 
the difficulty level a bit?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.390
Oh, yes, okay.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:12.300
They're really intrigued 
by your ability.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.020
I'm not sure how I should feel...

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.980
What is this?

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.780
S.   lactis  

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.780
I see these guys all the time.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.170
They're in yogurt, right?

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:28.010
That's right. It's yogurt.

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:31.410
Professor, anyone could figure 
that out with one look.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.230
Then let me ask you this, Sawaki-kun.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.670
This is also yogurt.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:40.420
They look identical, but they were 
made in different countries.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.020
One was made in Europe, 
the other in Japan.

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:45.850
Can you tell which one is Japanese?

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.050
What do you think, Sawaki?

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.000
Going by their features,

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.080
I'd say this one was made in Japan.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.030
How can you tell?

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.360
You could tell the difference 
in the lactic acid bacteria?

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:01.070
Sort of.

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:02.560
So, to your eyes,

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:05.090
there are clear differences even 
among the same types of microbes.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.570
Well...

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:10.470
I just thought from the start that 
these guys looked Japanese.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.610
That is so, it is.

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:13.450
L.   yogurti

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.630
Is it so?

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:13.450
It is so.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:15.980
By the way, can I ask a question?

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.310
What is it?

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.460
Huh? Me?

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:23.610
Is it okay to be in the 
lab without lab shoes on?

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:27.220
Why should it matter what shoes I wear?

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:29.720
I was just wondering.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:34.790
But that is wonderful, Sawaki-kun.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.120
You may even be able

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:39.820
to see microbes that haven't 
been discovered yet.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:41.610
If you study here,

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:41.480
L.    plantarum

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:44.480
we could make a Nobel 
Prize worthy discovery.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:47.740
Rice 
Bran

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:47.740
I still don't believe it.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:50.510
Sawaki-kun, look at this.

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:51.240
What is that?

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:54.830
This is vinegar, still in 
the fermenting process,

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.120
that was given to me 
by a distillery in Hida.

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:57.920
Vinegar?

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:58.960
Yes.

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:01.420
Oh, look.

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:03.170
A.   aceti

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.550
I think this one is supposed 
to be in vinegar.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:09.990
But it's not, so that 
must be mirin, right?

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:13.680
It really is an acetobacter!

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:15.740
I can't believe it...

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:18.460
You're saying you snatched 
a microbe out of the air?

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.190
Well, yeah...

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:23.190
That is a remarkable ability!

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.940
No way! It can't be true!

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:27.820
Sheesh...

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.730
Being able to see microbes caused 
me enough grief back home.

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:31.980
I have to deal with it here, too?

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.950
Maybe we should get going...

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:38.080
Sorry, Sawaki-kun, but I'd like 
you to stay here a bit longer.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.080
I have to do more?

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:43.400
Now, look at this.

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:46.670
It's a photo of malt fungi as seen 
through an electron microscope.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:49.780
You can see these with the naked eye?

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:50.690
Yeah...

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.470
They don't look like that, though.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.010
Then draw a picture of what 
they look like to you.

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.060
Sort of like this, I guess.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.620
What the hell is that?

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.810
That's supposed to be a microbe? 
You must be joking!

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.620
I'm sorry, but I just can't believe you.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:12.320
Wild guesses mean nothing to me.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.820
This is a petri dish culture.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:19.360
Can you tell what the microbes 
in this colony are?

00:16:20.920 --> 00:16:22.710
I haven't actually studied them,

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.350
so I don't know exactly what they are...

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.840
Oh, but I've seen these before.

00:16:28.310 --> 00:16:29.320
That's it!

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:31.720
I always saw them in public 
restrooms back home!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.580
Wait a minute!

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:35.900
What do they look like to you?

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:40.220
B.halodurans

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:38.300
Come on!

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.220
Oops, I landed on both feet!

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:42.430
They're playing S-ken.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.980
S-ken is a game that involves hopping on one foot to retrieve the opposing team's treasure.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:43.980
S-ken?

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.480
Stop playing around!

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:50.710
Do you realize how small 
alkalophilic bacteria are?!

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:53.490
Well... I told you, I haven't 
actually studied them...

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:57.000
You're lying! Microbes playing S-ken...

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.730
That's ridiculous!

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:01.360
You're obviously making this stuff up!

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.080
Next, what are these microbes?

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:05.500
B.   natto

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:05.460
Oh, they're the ones you find on natto.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:06.830
Then what about these?

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:06.830
S.   cerevisiae

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:08.390
Those are in bakeries.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:09.710
Then what about these?

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.740
Answer them all!

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:14.720
Are you serious?

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.440
She's scary...

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.220
Hey, we're gonna be stared at!

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.100
Even the microbes are scared.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:24.100
Are you trying to tell me you 
know what they're feeling?!

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:26.880
Well... uh, I mean...

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.360
Um, let's stop here for today.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.360
I...

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.830
I'll never accept this.

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:37.370
You're saying you can see all 
the microbes in the world?

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:39.890
The same microbes that 
humans have invested

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.480
so much time in discovering 
little by little?

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:45.700
This kid who knows nothing 
about them compared to me?

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:47.750
Looks like it was a pretty 
big shock for her.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.630
Um, I'm sick of this.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:52.250
Mind if I do something sort of rude?

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:53.510
What?

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.270
What's with you? Got a bondage fetish?

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:12.150
T.   rubrum

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:10.070
Let's build ourselves a house here!

00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:12.150
I'm gonna get my own room, too!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:16.030
Hasegawa-san, you're okay for now.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.920
All you need is to keep 
them dry and clean,

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:22.030
and to get a good prescription.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:23.540
Athlete's Foot

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:28.630
Are you convinced, Hasegawa-kun?

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:30.040
Yes.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:35.830
H-Hey, Kei!

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.430
There're hiochi bacteria in here!

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:37.880
What?!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.430
That's bad!

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:42.140
If I carry hiochi back home, 
my family will kill me!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.780
They're outside the window!

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:56.740
Can you tell where they're 
coming from, Sawaki?

00:18:58.250 --> 00:18:59.450
There, Kei!

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.950
Hiochi are pouring out of that window!

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.120
There are so many...

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:14.230
He can see microbes and 
even tell how they feel?

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:15.780
That's just...

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:17.590
I just can't accept it.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.560
That's the trouble with you 
still being so immature.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:25.800
If you get all bent out of shape by 
our precious experimental subject,

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:27.220
we'll be left with nothing.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.810
Even mice produce the best 
results if you raise them

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.350
with love and care.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.180
Look at the bigger picture.

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:37.300
There's no need to rush.

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:40.110
Okay.

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:27.410
Microbe Theater!

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:27.430
Moyashimon

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:27.430
Episode 1

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.430
Microbe Theater

00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:40.130
We're gonna brew!

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:41.340
We're gonna brew!

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:42.570
We're gonna brew!

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:44.450
Who are you guys?

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:45.410
I'm Oryzae!

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:46.460
I'm Oryzae!

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.360
Oryzae

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:47.620
I'm Oryzae!

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:49.310
So, where are we?

00:21:49.310 --> 00:21:50.470
This is a moyashiya!

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:51.300
Moyashiya!

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:53.310
What's a moyashiya?

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:55.080
A place where malt fungi are made!

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:56.580
Malt fungi?

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:57.830
Miso...

00:21:58.450 --> 00:21:59.550
Soy sauce...

00:21:59.990 --> 00:22:01.090
And sake...

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:03.560
We're the microbes that make them all!

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:05.260
You're increasing so fast.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.720
We'll keep increasing!

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:07.930
And what about you?

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:09.510
Who are you?

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:12.600
Chrysogenum 
Blue Mold

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:11.240
I'm Chrysogenum,

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:12.590
a blue mold.

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:14.840
Blue mold?

00:22:14.840 --> 00:22:16.310
Eww!

00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:21.570
Like you stupid fungi know anything.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:23.750
You're a fungus, too!

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:31.160
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 2,

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:31.160
